TEXT 96 48 Left 3 ;#406 Current mirror and current multiplier
TEXT 96 112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VXZH3UE-kSw
TEXT 96 160 Left 2 ;A 2 mA current regulator diode feeds a transistor mirror, and unequal emitter resistors multiply the output current.
TEXT 96 752 Left 2 ;Vsense is a zero-volt ammeter in place of the meter on Alan's drawing. Sweeping the rail to its
TEXT 96 784 Left 2 ;12 V operating point shows the reference branch coming into regulation before the output branch.
